"""odeck-10 routing, phase g: front block local nets (card reader GL3224 + SD/microSD, USB-A port electronics).

NETS = [] / GROUPED: everything drawn here lives in group "route:g_front"; only that group is replaced on re-run
(nets are shared with b_power / e_hs_eth_sd / f_fanout / z_stitch).

What is routed (see docs/routing-notes/g_front.md):
- U901 (GL3224, bottom) local pins: CR_3V3 / CR_1V2 LDO rails to their caps and to each other, VUHS1/2, crystal
  (XI/XO <= 4 mm, B.Cu), straps, LED, SD detect / WP (via d_hs_hub's reserved toe vias), microSD CDZ and the
  CR_USD_VCC run to J902 (B.Cu south of the USB-A shell tabs, clear of the L3 microSD band).
- USB-A ports: SW_IN bulk/HF caps to the SW_IN node, EN (OR gate -> TPS2553 + pull-down), ILIM, INA180 output ->
  ISENSE filter, VBUS clamp (D702/D704 pin 5) to the +5V_USBAx pour, local +3V3 (OR gate / INA180) fed from the
  right block's L4 +3V3 plane.
- Unconnected supply pads in the region (GND C914.2 boxed in -> 0.351/0.15 via-in-pad like f_fanout's VIP).

The geometry below was generated by a grid A* router (0.025 mm grid, 0.15 mm clearance + 0.02 mm margin, 0.3 mm to
USB_90/HS_85 tracks and HV copper, region-clipped) run against the board after a_planes..f_fanout, then frozen here.
Each entry: (name, net, width, [(layer, [points])], [via points], (via size, drill)).
"""

